{"tool_name":"cecaflux","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cecaflux","home":"https://www.cecaflux.net","license":"Not licensed","summary":"Web server for standardized and visual instationary 13C metabolic flux analysis.","addition_date":"2022-08-13T04:20:21.188007Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:50:02.237911Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cecaflux","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Zhentao Liu"},{"name":"Tie Shen","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7313-3494"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Metabolic labeling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3715"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"CeCaFLUX","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btac341","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: The number of instationary 13C-metabolic flux (INST-MFA) studies grows every year, making it more important than ever to ensure the clarity, standardization and reproducibility of each study. We proposed CeCaFLUX, the first user-friendly web server that derives metabolic flux distribution from instationary 13C-labeled data. Flux optimization and statistical analysis are achieved through an evolutionary optimization in a parallel manner. It can visualize the flux optimizing process in real-Time and the ultimate flux outcome. It will also function as a database to enhance the consistency and to facilitate sharing of flux studies.","authors":[{"name":"Chen Z."},{"name":"Liang S."},{"name":"Liu Z."},{"name":"Shen T."},{"name":"Xie X."},{"name":"Zhang Z."}],"date":"2022-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"CeCaFLUX: The first web server for standardized and visual instationary 13C metabolic flux analysis"},"pmid":"35595250"}],"topic":[{"term